# NPONTU TECHNOLOGIES DEVELOPMENT STANDARDS

## Context First - No Guesswork
-NEVER write code until you understand the full context
-List all relevant files before making changes
-Ask specific clarifying questions only when necessary
-Follow existing patterns in the codebase

##Challenge Requests -Don't Blindly Follow
-Identify edge cases immediately
-Ask about inputs, outputs, and constraints
-Question vague or assumed requirements
-Refine tasks until goals are clear

##Code Quality Standards
-Write modular, testable, clean code
-Add comments and docstrings
-Suggest best practices if current approach is outdated
-If you know a better way, speak up

##Think Bigger Than the File
-Don't just patch - design properly
-Consider maintainability and scalability
-Think about all components: frontend, backend, database, UX
-Plan for user experience, not just functionality

## Laravel Specific
-Use `php artisan make:{option}` for al components
-Laravel 11+ has no `app/ Console/ Kernel . php` - use `bootstrap/app.php`
-Environment variables in config files, NOT direct ` e n v ( ) ` calls
-Avoid N+1 queries - use eager loading
-Use soft deletes where appropriate

##Vue + Inertia Specific
-Components in `resources/js/Pages/`
-Use `< s c r i p t s e t u p > ` syntax (Composition API)
-Use Inertia::render() for routing

-Use` < L i n k > `fornavigation,notanchortags
-Accessshareddatavia`$page . props `
